@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Refresh popularity counts
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
box "Backend — Logos Lab Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ContentPopularityRefreshJob" as ContentPopularityRefreshJob
  participant "ContentRepository" as ContentRepository
end box
box "Backend — Logos Lab Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  queue "Job queue" as queue
  database "Logos Lab database" as db
end box
queue -> ContentPopularityRefreshJob : Deliver refresh message (interval TO SUPPLY)
ContentPopularityRefreshJob -> ContentRepository : Recompute popularity for 30-day window (L2-002)
ContentRepository -> db : Count distinct members with engagement per item since now minus 30 days
db --> ContentRepository : Counts per item
ContentRepository -> db : Upsert content_popularity in one transaction
db --> ContentRepository : Commit
ContentRepository --> ContentPopularityRefreshJob : Rows updated
ContentPopularityRefreshJob --> queue : Acknowledge message (idempotent; retried with backoff on failure)
@enduml
